Defect: SMI-UNEXPORTED-IMPORT https://pysnmp.github.io/pysmi/stable/mib-defects.html#smi-unexported-import

The module imports Unsigned32 FROM CISCO-TC, which does not export it.
CISCO-TC's own revision history records adding an Unsigned32 textual
convention in 1996 and removing it again in 2004 -- the removal correct,
since RFC 2578 had made Unsigned32 a base type of SNMPv2-SMI in between.
This module was never revised to follow, so the import names an export
that was real when it was written.

The repair takes Unsigned32 from SNMPv2-SMI, which the clause already
imports from, and drops the CISCO-TC line.

--- a/CISCO-ENTITY-ALARM-MIB
+++ b/CISCO-ENTITY-ALARM-MIB
@@ -13,7 +13,8 @@
     Gauge32,
     MODULE-IDENTITY,
     NOTIFICATION-TYPE,
-    OBJECT-TYPE                         FROM SNMPv2-SMI
+    OBJECT-TYPE,
+    Unsigned32                         FROM SNMPv2-SMI
     TEXTUAL-CONVENTION,
     AutonomousType,
     DisplayString,
@@ -27,7 +28,6 @@
     entPhysicalIndex,
     PhysicalIndex                       FROM ENTITY-MIB
     ciscoMgmt                           FROM CISCO-SMI
-    Unsigned32                          FROM CISCO-TC
     ;
 
 ciscoEntityAlarmMIB MODULE-IDENTITY
